 "title": "Спор про кокосы  (The Coconut Bet)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "barinov": "Шеф",
  "fedya": "Федя",
  "senya": "Сеня"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "In the kitchen, Fedya reads a bizarre statistic about falling coconuts while Senya brags that a coconut could never knock him out, leading to a reckless bet right as Chef Barinov speaks with the inspector.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "От падения кокосов гибнут люди.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Что это за полный бред?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "На меня кокос уже падал.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Ну я же совсем живой.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Ты не выдержишь удар кокосом.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Я не выдержу такой удар?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Давай тогда с тобой замажем.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Так я получу эту звезду?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Надеюсь, у нас будет отлично.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Кокосы никогда не предупреждают заранее.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Можешь бросить в меня кокос.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Может завтра, а может сейчас.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "От падения кокосов гибнут люди.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'People die from falling coconuts.' Highlighting the fall in the exchange, Fedya uses \"padeniya\" (\"fall\", from \"padeniye\") to make the point stick.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Что это за полный бред?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What kind of total nonsense is this?' Senya tests straight out what Fedya is actually getting at here.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "На меня кокос уже падал.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'A coconut has already fallen on me.' Addressing a coconut on the spot, Senya centers the remark on \"kokos\" (\"coconut\") without any extra fuss.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Ну я же совсем живой.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Well, I am completely alive.' Emphasizing how alive he is during the talk, Senya adds \"sovsem\" (\"completely, at all\") so the statement leaves zero room for doubt.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Ты не выдержишь удар кокосом.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You will not withstand a blow from a coconut.' Fedya proceeds right away around Senya, shifting the mood of the conversation in a single beat.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Я не выдержу такой удар?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I will not withstand such a blow?' Bringing up a blow to Fedya, Senya uses \"vyderzhu\" (\"I will endure\", from \"vyderzhat\") to make the point stick.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Давай тогда с тобой замажем.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Let us make a bet then.' Cutting in quietly before Senya, Fedya starts with \"davay\" (\"come on, let's\") to invite Senya right into the action.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Так я получу эту звезду?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'So will I get this star?' Barinov tests firmly if there is more going on behind the scenes.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Надеюсь, у нас будет отлично.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I hope everything will be great for us.' Barinov jumps in dryly during the talk and brings in \"otlichno\" (\"perfect, great\") to make the meaning unmistakable.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Кокосы никогда не предупреждают заранее.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Coconuts never warn you in advance.' Pushing back earnestly in the exchange, Fedya pairs the negative word with \"ne\" (\"not\"), since Russian naturally doubles its negatives for emphasis.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Можешь бросить в меня кокос.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You can throw a coconut at me.' Addressing a coconut hearing Fedya, Senya puts the real issue right on the table for Fedya.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Может завтра, а может сейчас.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Maybe tomorrow, or maybe right now.' Fedya replies decisively with Senya and leans on \"zavtra\" (\"tomorrow\") to give the whole sentence its punch.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "От падения кокосов гибнут люди.",
   "gap": 0.5
